  "imageName": "person.2.circle.fill",
  "intro": "Personal pronouns change dramatically across cases - much more than nouns! Меня and мне are different forms of 'me'. After prepositions, third-person pronouns add н-: его → у него, ей → к ней. In Part 1 we focus on four cases: Nominative, Accusative, Genitive, and Dative.",
  "rules": [
    "After prepositions, 3rd person pronouns add н-: его → у него, ей → к ней. Without a preposition, no н-: я вижу его.",
    "Genitive and accusative share the same forms for all pronouns: меня, тебя, его, её, нас, вас, их.",
    "The reflexive pronoun себя (oneself) declines like ты: себя, себе — but has no nominative form.",
    "Мы and вы follow a neat parallel: нас/вас, нам/вам — the pattern makes both easy to learn together."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Он видит меня. (He sees me.), accusative",
    "Дай мне книгу. (Give me the book.), dative",
    "У него есть машина. (He has a car.), genitive with preposition",
    "Позвони ему. (Call him.), dative without preposition"
  ],
